# Basic Excel Formulas


| Formula    | Syntax                            | Purpose                         |
| -----------| ----------------------------------| ------------------------------- |
| SUM        | =SUM(number1, [number2], ...)     | Adds numbers                    |
| AVERAGE    | =AVERAGE(number1, [number2], ...) | Finds average                   |
| COUNT      | =COUNT(value1, [value2], ...)     | Counts cells containing numbers |
| COUNTA     | =COUNTA(value1, [value2], ...)    | Counts non-empty cells          |
| COUNTBLANK | =COUNTBLANK(range)`               | Counts blank cells              |
| MAX        | =MAX(number1, [number2], ...)     | Finds highest value             |
| MIN        | =MIN(number1, [number2], ...)     | Finds lowest value              |
| LARGE      | =LARGE(array, k)                  | Finds the kth largest value     |
| SMALL      | =SMALL(array, k)                  | Finds the kth smallest value    |
| ABS        | =ABS(number)                      | Returns absolute value          |


Conditional / Logical Formulas

| Formula | Syntax                                                    | Purpose                           |
| --------| ----------------------------------------------------------| ----------------------------------|
| IF      | =IF(logical_test, value_if_true, value_if_false)          | Checks a condition                |
| IFS     | =IFS(logical_test1, value1, [logical_test2, value2], ...) | Checks multiple conditions        |
| AND     | =AND(logical1, [logical2], ...)                           | Checks if all conditions are TRUE |
| OR      | =OR(logical1, [logical2], ...)                            | Checks if any condition is TRUE   |
| NOT     | =NOT(logical)                                             | Reverses TRUE/FALSE               |
| IFERROR | =IFERROR(value, value_if_error)                           | Handles errors                    |



Conditional Calculation

| Formula    | Syntax                                                                                    | Purpose                                   |
| -----------| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------| ------------------------------------------|
| SUMIF      | =SUMIF(range, criteria, [sum_range])                                                      | Adds values based on one condition         |
| SUMIFS     | =SUMIFS(sum_range, criteria_range1, criteria1, [criteria_range2, criteria2], ...)         | Adds values based on multiple conditions   |
| COUNTIF    | =COUNTIF(range, criteria)                                                                 | Counts based on one condition              |
| COUNTIFS   | =COUNTIFS(criteria_range1, criteria1, [criteria_range2, criteria2], ...)                  | Counts based on multiple conditions        |
| AVERAGEIF  | =AVERAGEIF(range, criteria, [average_range])                                              | Finds average based on one condition       |
| AVERAGEIFS | =AVERAGEIFS(average_range, criteria_range1, criteria1, [criteria_range2, criteria2], ...) | Finds average based on multiple conditions |

Syntax notation
range → cells/range to work with
number / value → value or cell reference
criteria → condition used for filtering
... → additional arguments can be added

Text Formulas

| Formula    | Syntax                                                  | Purpose                           |
| -----------| --------------------------------------------------------| ----------------------------------|
| LEFT       | =LEFT(text, [num_chars])                                | Gets characters from left         |
| RIGHT      | =RIGHT(text, [num_chars])                               | Gets characters from right        |
| MID        | =MID(text, start_num, num_chars)                        | Gets characters from middle       |
| LEN        | =LEN(text)                                              | Counts characters                 |
| TRIM       | =TRIM(text)                                             | Removes extra spaces              |
| UPPER      | =UPPER(text)                                            | Converts text to uppercase        |
| LOWER      | =LOWER(text)                                            | Converts text to lowercase        |
| PROPER     | =PROPER(text)`                                          | Capitalizes first letter of words |
| CONCAT     | =CONCAT(text1, [text2], ...)                            | Combines text                     |
| TEXTJOIN   | =TEXTJOIN(delimiter, ignore_empty, text1, [text2], ...) | Combines text with a delimiter    |
| FIND       | =FIND(find_text, within_text, [start_num])              | Finds position of text            |
| SEARCH     | =SEARCH(find_text, within_text, [start_num])            | Searches for text                 |
| SUBSTITUTE | =SUBSTITUTE(text, old_text, new_text, [instance_num])   | Replaces specific text            |
| TEXT       | =TEXT(value, format_text)                               | Formats value as text             |


Date & Time Formulas

| Formula | Syntax                                 | Purpose                             |
| --------| ---------------------------------------| ----------------------------------- |
| TODAY   | =TODAY()                               | Returns current date                |
| NOW     | =NOW()                                 | Returns current date and time       |
| DATE    | =DATE(year, month, day)                | Creates a date                      |
| DAY     | =DAY(serial_number)                    | Extracts day                        |
| MONTH   | =MONTH(serial_number)                  | Extracts month                      |
| YEAR    | =YEAR(serial_number)                   | Extracts year                       |
| WEEKDAY | =WEEKDAY(serial_number, [return_type]) | Returns weekday number              |
| WEEKNUM | =WEEKNUM(serial_number, [return_type]) | Returns week number                 |
| DATEDIF | =DATEDIF(start_date, end_date, unit)   | Calculates difference between dates |
| EDATE   | =EDATE(start_date, months)             | Adds/subtracts months               |
| EOMONTH | =EOMONTH(start_date, months)           | Returns month-end date              |


Lookup Formulas

| Formula       | Syntax                                                                                          | Purpose                     |
| --------------| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------| --------------------------- |
| VLOOKUP       | =VLOOKUP(lookup_value, table_array, col_index_num, [range_lookup])                              | Searches vertically         |
| HLOOKUP       | =HLOOKUP(lookup_value, table_array, row_index_num, [range_lookup])                              | Searches horizontally       |
| XLOOKUP       | =XLOOKUP(lookup_value, lookup_array, return_array, [if_not_found], [match_mode], [search_mode]) | Modern lookup formula       |
| INDEX         | =INDEX(array, row_num, [column_num])                                                            | Returns value at a position |
| MATCH         | =MATCH(lookup_value, lookup_array, [match_type])                                                | Finds position of a value   |
| INDEX + MATCH | =INDEX(return_array, MATCH(lookup_value, lookup_array, [match_type]))                           | Flexible lookup             |

Dynamic Array Formulas

| Formula  | Syntax                                                                  | Purpose                     |
| ---------| ------------------------------------------------------------------------| --------------------------- |
| SEQUENCE | =SEQUENCE(rows, [columns], [start], [step])                             | Generates a number sequence |
| FILTER   | =FILTER(array, include, [if_empty])                                     | Filters data                |
| SORT     | =SORT(array, [sort_index], [sort_order], [by_col])                      | Sorts data                  |
| SORTBY   | =SORTBY(array, by_array1, [sort_order1], [by_array2, sort_order2], ...) | Sorts using another range   |
| UNIQUE   | =UNIQUE(array, [by_col], [exactly_once])                                | Returns unique values       |




